35,2,1,talk,Rin,,"The all-in rates are so simple! Even if some eat more, the price is fixed. I love that!","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Great. Meanwhile, the ferry option is a nightmare. We'd lose two whole days just to transit.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Rin, simplicity is good, but all-in rates can be unfair. However, they prevent the chaos of splitting individual bills.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Takumi,,The inn sounds like a disaster. Everyone in one room on futons? And strict meal times? No way.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"It seems we have a choice between a shared house, a town inn, or a remote villa. Each changes our dynamic.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Takumi, if we get a whole house, we can just do whatever we want! And the price is clear.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Toshio, the ""dynamic"" doesn't matter if we spend the whole trip waiting for a bus or a ferry.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"The offshore house is 5,400 yen per person. If we book the whole place, the cost is predictable and equal.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Rin, the house only has one bathroom for all of us. That's just as bad as the inn.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Shunichi, efficiency is a tool, not the goal. If we are too efficient, we might feel crowded or disconnected.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Rin,,I don't mind the bathroom if I know exactly how much money I need to bring!,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,I'm leaning toward the city option. Trains every few minutes mean zero planning and zero waiting.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"The city option usually means separate rooms, which leads to the ""who pays for what"" problem again.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Takumi,,The city option has separate rooms and no fixed meal times. That's the only way I'm sleeping.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Toshio,,Last year we were too separate. A house might be too crowded. A town with an inn might be the middle ground.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
